@TrainBooking.Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5255

# Note: ids below assume a fresh database (Postgres identity columns don't
# reset after a delete). If you've already created/deleted trains or tickets,
# adjust the ids in the URLs/bodies to match what GET /api/trains actually returns.

### 1. Create a train -> expect 201
POST {{TrainBooking.Api_HostAddress}}/api/trains
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "trainNumber": "12951",
  "trainName": "Mumbai Rajdhani",
  "source": "Mumbai Central",
  "destination": "New Delhi",
  "capacity": 72
}

### 2. List all trains -> expect 200
GET {{TrainBooking.Api_HostAddress}}/api/trains
Accept: application/json

### 3. Get train by id -> expect 200
GET {{TrainBooking.Api_HostAddress}}/api/trains/1
Accept: application/json

### 4. Book seat 5 on train 1 -> expect 201
POST {{TrainBooking.Api_HostAddress}}/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "trainId": 1,
  "passengerName": "Asha Rao",
  "seatNumber": 5
}

### 5. Attempt to double-book seat 5 -> expect 409 Conflict
POST {{TrainBooking.Api_HostAddress}}/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "trainId": 1,
  "passengerName": "Vikram Shah",
  "seatNumber": 5
}

### 6. Book without a seat number -> expect 201, auto-assigned to the lowest free seat
POST {{TrainBooking.Api_HostAddress}}/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "trainId": 1,
  "passengerName": "Auto Assigned"
}

### 7. Cancel ticket 1 (the seat-5 booking from step 4) -> expect 200, status Cancelled
POST {{TrainBooking.Api_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/1/cancel

### 8. Re-book seat 5 on train 1 -> expect 201 (proves cancellation freed the seat)
POST {{TrainBooking.Api_HostAddress}}/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "trainId": 1,
  "passengerName": "Vikram Shah",
  "seatNumber": 5
}

### 9. List tickets for train 1 -> confirm one Cancelled + two Booked
GET {{TrainBooking.Api_HostAddress}}/api/tickets?trainId=1
Accept: application/json

### 10. Update the train -> expect 200
PUT {{TrainBooking.Api_HostAddress}}/api/trains/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "trainNumber": "12951",
  "trainName": "Mumbai Rajdhani Express",
  "source": "Mumbai Central",
  "destination": "New Delhi",
  "capacity": 80
}

### 11. Delete the train while bookings are still active -> expect 409 (delete guard)
DELETE {{TrainBooking.Api_HostAddress}}/api/trains/1

### 12. Cancel the remaining active tickets (2 and 3), then delete succeeds -> expect 204
POST {{TrainBooking.Api_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/2/cancel

###
POST {{TrainBooking.Api_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/3/cancel

###
DELETE {{TrainBooking.Api_HostAddress}}/api/trains/1
